1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,546
When's the last time you said
thank you and really meant it?

2
00:00:03,918 --> 00:00:08,048
I don't mean the one you toss at the
cashier on your way out the door.

3
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:10,601
I mean the kind where it hits you that

4
00:00:10,601 --> 00:00:13,183
somebody gave you
something you did not earn.

5
00:00:14,305 --> 00:00:17,038
Most of us do our biggest thanking of the

6
00:00:17,038 --> 00:00:19,970
year about four seconds
before dinner today.

7
00:00:20,342 --> 00:00:23,966
Somebody clears their throat,
everybody's looking at

8
00:00:23,966 --> 00:00:27,730
the gravy, and the amen comes
out like a starting gun.

9
00:00:28,102 --> 00:00:32,798
Ten lepers got healed one day, and
only one came back to say thank you.

10
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:36,696
Today I want to give
that word a few minutes.

11
00:00:37,068 --> 00:00:37,819
Thanks.

12
00:00:38,191 --> 00:00:42,080
The Bible has a lot more to say
about it than we usually do,

13
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:45,903
and I think it might change
how you sit down at that table.

14
00:00:47,725 --> 00:00:51,872
Open your Bible with me
to Psalm 107, verse 1.

15
00:00:53,444 --> 00:00:58,694
O give thanks unto the LORD, for he is
good: for his mercy endureth for ever.

16
00:01:00,134 --> 00:01:02,040
The psalm gives two reasons.

17
00:01:02,412 --> 00:01:05,517
He is good, and His
mercy does not run out.

18
00:01:05,889 --> 00:01:09,302
It doesn't wait for a good
year before it asks for thanks.

19
00:01:09,674 --> 00:01:14,814
It hangs the whole thing on who He is,
and He was the same on your worst day.

20
00:01:15,936 --> 00:01:18,965
Think about the last time
you were truly thankful.

21
00:01:19,337 --> 00:01:22,432
Maybe somebody covered a
bill you couldn't, or a

22
00:01:22,432 --> 00:01:25,527
friend drove two hours
when they didn't have to.

23
00:01:25,899 --> 00:01:27,950
What was going on inside you?

24
00:01:28,322 --> 00:01:31,132
You felt small and glad at the same time.

25
00:01:31,504 --> 00:01:34,136
Small, because you knew
you hadn't earned it.

26
00:01:34,508 --> 00:01:36,519
Glad, because it came anyway.

27
00:01:37,641 --> 00:01:39,457
That's what thankfulness is.

28
00:01:39,829 --> 00:01:42,629
Humility and gladness in one heart.

29
00:01:43,001 --> 00:01:46,321
A proud man can be happy
about what he gets, but he

30
00:01:46,321 --> 00:01:49,900
can't be thankful, because
he figures he had it coming.

31
00:01:50,272 --> 00:01:55,118
You have to know you got more than you
deserved before the word means anything.

32
00:01:55,490 --> 00:01:58,084
And that's the exact word the psalm uses.

33
00:01:58,456 --> 00:01:59,330
Mercy.

34
00:01:59,702 --> 00:02:01,435
Getting what you didn't earn.

35
00:02:03,257 --> 00:02:07,138
Jesus saw this play out one
day, and Luke wrote it down.

36
00:02:07,510 --> 00:02:09,262
Luke chapter 17.

37
00:02:09,634 --> 00:02:13,694
He's heading into a village and
ten men with leprosy meet Him.

38
00:02:14,066 --> 00:02:18,226
They stand way off, because the
law kept them away from everybody.

39
00:02:18,598 --> 00:02:20,378
Family, work, worship.

40
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:23,943
And they lift their voices
and ask for one thing.

41
00:02:25,515 --> 00:02:28,099
Jesus, Master, have mercy on us.

42
00:02:29,539 --> 00:02:30,634
Have mercy.

43
00:02:31,006 --> 00:02:32,670
Same word as the psalm.

44
00:02:33,042 --> 00:02:36,159
He tells them to go show
themselves to the priests.

45
00:02:36,531 --> 00:02:38,499
Nobody gets healed first.

46
00:02:38,871 --> 00:02:43,614
They turn and start walking on His word,
and somewhere on the road it happens.

47
00:02:43,986 --> 00:02:45,120
They're cleansed.

48
00:02:45,492 --> 00:02:46,476
All ten.

49
00:02:47,598 --> 00:02:51,319
Now Luke tells us what came
next, and I'll read it straight.

50
00:02:52,891 --> 00:02:56,930
And one of them, when he saw
that he was healed, turned back,

51
00:02:56,930 --> 00:03:00,704
and with a loud voice glorified
God, And fell down on his

52
00:03:00,704 --> 00:03:04,677
face at his feet, giving him
thanks: and he was a Samaritan.

53
00:03:06,117 --> 00:03:07,403
One out of ten.

54
00:03:07,775 --> 00:03:09,424
And Jesus noticed.

55
00:03:10,996 --> 00:03:14,207
Were there not ten cleansed?
but where are the nine?

56
00:03:16,347 --> 00:03:19,211
The Bible doesn't tell
us where the nine went.

57
00:03:19,583 --> 00:03:22,556
I'll tell you what I think,
and I'm guessing here.

58
00:03:22,928 --> 00:03:24,986
I don't think they were bad men.

59
00:03:25,358 --> 00:03:27,077
They'd been cut off for years.

60
00:03:27,449 --> 00:03:32,397
They had families to find, a priest
to see, a whole life to catch up on.

61
00:03:32,769 --> 00:03:33,904
They were busy.

62
00:03:34,276 --> 00:03:37,786
All of them did what Jesus
said and kept walking.

63
00:03:38,908 --> 00:03:40,891
That's why this one gets me.

64
00:03:41,263 --> 00:03:45,036
Most days I'd be one of the
nine, and I bet you would too.

65
00:03:45,408 --> 00:03:47,883
Nobody decides to be ungrateful.

66
00:03:48,255 --> 00:03:52,437
We get busy, and by Thursday
the gift is just how things are.

67
00:03:53,559 --> 00:03:58,103
Jesus had one more thing to say, and
it went to the man who came back.

68
00:03:59,675 --> 00:04:03,237
Arise, go thy way: thy
faith hath made thee whole.

69
00:04:04,677 --> 00:04:05,969
Ten got healed.

70
00:04:06,341 --> 00:04:09,548
One got to hear Jesus
say he was made whole.

71
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:12,009
The nine walked off with the gift.

72
00:04:12,381 --> 00:04:14,132
He walked off with the Giver.

73
00:04:15,954 --> 00:04:17,727
David knew we'd forget.

74
00:04:18,099 --> 00:04:22,967
Listen to what he told his own
soul in Psalm 103, verse 2.

75
00:04:24,539 --> 00:04:28,749
Bless the LORD, O my soul, and
forget not all his benefits:

76
00:04:30,189 --> 00:04:31,353
Forget not.

77
00:04:31,725 --> 00:04:34,030
A king had to say that to himself.

78
00:04:34,402 --> 00:04:38,053
So we can quit acting like
thankfulness comes naturally.

79
00:04:39,175 --> 00:04:40,975
What's on your table today?

80
00:04:41,347 --> 00:04:42,546
The food, sure.

81
00:04:42,918 --> 00:04:44,422
The people around it.

82
00:04:44,794 --> 00:04:48,637
The job that paid for the food,
the truck that got you there.

83
00:04:49,009 --> 00:04:51,784
James tells us where all of it comes from.

84
00:04:52,156 --> 00:04:54,832
James chapter 1, verse 17.

85
00:04:56,404 --> 00:05:01,505
Every good gift and every perfect gift
is from above, and cometh down from the

86
00:05:01,505 --> 00:05:06,345
Father of lights, with whom is no
variableness, neither shadow of turning.

87
00:05:07,785 --> 00:05:09,687
Everything good comes down.

88
00:05:10,059 --> 00:05:12,406
Thanksgiving is how it goes back up.

89
00:05:12,778 --> 00:05:16,574
Somebody gave you something,
and you turn around and say so.

90
00:05:16,946 --> 00:05:18,694
That finishes the circle.

91
00:05:19,066 --> 00:05:21,959
Leave it off and the gift
just sits in your hand

92
00:05:21,959 --> 00:05:24,792
while you start to think
you built it yourself.

93
00:05:26,614 --> 00:05:30,563
Paul traced a lot of what goes
wrong with people back to this spot.

94
00:05:30,935 --> 00:05:33,647
Romans chapter 1, verse 21.

95
00:05:35,219 --> 00:05:39,069
Because that, when they knew
God, they glorified him not

96
00:05:39,069 --> 00:05:42,850
as God, neither were thankful;
but became vain in their

97
00:05:42,850 --> 00:05:46,357
imaginations, and their
foolish heart was darkened.

98
00:05:47,797 --> 00:05:49,315
Neither were thankful.

99
00:05:49,687 --> 00:05:52,526
The slide started when
they quit saying thanks.

100
00:05:52,898 --> 00:05:55,100
The big wicked stuff came after.

101
00:05:56,922 --> 00:06:01,124
Now thankfulness does something
for you too, and I'm glad it does.

102
00:06:01,496 --> 00:06:06,486
Paul wrote about worry in Philippians
chapter 4, verses 6 and 7.

103
00:06:08,058 --> 00:06:11,855
Be careful for nothing; but
in every thing by prayer and

104
00:06:11,855 --> 00:06:16,060
supplication with thanksgiving
let your requests be made known

105
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:20,400
unto God. And the peace of God,
which passeth all understanding,

106
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:24,062
shall keep your hearts and
minds through Christ Jesus.

107
00:06:25,502 --> 00:06:26,912
See where the thanks sits?

108
00:06:27,284 --> 00:06:29,332
Right in the middle of the asking.

109
00:06:29,704 --> 00:06:34,034
Bring the request, and bring the
thank you with it, in the same prayer.

110
00:06:34,406 --> 00:06:38,482
Then the peace of God stands guard
over your heart and your mind.

111
00:06:39,604 --> 00:06:42,870
People who study this keep
finding the same thing.

112
00:06:43,242 --> 00:06:47,233
Folks who make a habit of giving
thanks tend to sleep better.

113
00:06:47,605 --> 00:06:48,783
They worry less.

114
00:06:49,155 --> 00:06:50,686
Their friendships last.

115
00:06:51,058 --> 00:06:55,944
They bounce back quicker when life knocks
them down, and they get more generous.

116
00:06:56,316 --> 00:06:59,163
The researchers are
catching up to something

117
00:06:59,163 --> 00:07:02,076
Paul wrote down about
two thousand years ago.

118
00:07:02,448 --> 00:07:06,654
Thanks doesn't replace a doctor,
and nobody should tell you it does.

119
00:07:07,026 --> 00:07:12,041
God did build us so a thankful heart
runs better than a bitter one, though.

120
00:07:13,863 --> 00:07:18,159
Then there's the verse people throw
at you when you're having a bad week.

121
00:07:18,531 --> 00:07:22,094
First Thessalonians chapter 5, verse 18.

122
00:07:23,666 --> 00:07:26,664
In every thing give
thanks: for this is the

123
00:07:26,664 --> 00:07:29,662
will of God in Christ
Jesus concerning you.

124
00:07:31,102 --> 00:07:33,105
Look at the little word in there.

125
00:07:33,477 --> 00:07:34,160
In.

126
00:07:34,532 --> 00:07:36,345
It says in every thing.

127
00:07:36,717 --> 00:07:38,740
It doesn't say for every thing.

128
00:07:39,112 --> 00:07:41,454
You don't have to call a bad day good.

129
00:07:41,826 --> 00:07:46,102
You can look around in the middle of
it and find what He still gave you.

130
00:07:46,474 --> 00:07:49,416
A paycheck that came
in short, but it came.

131
00:07:49,788 --> 00:07:51,865
A person who picked up the phone.

132
00:07:52,987 --> 00:07:55,802
If there's an empty
chair at your table this

133
00:07:55,802 --> 00:07:58,232
year, you don't have to fake anything.

134
00:07:58,604 --> 00:08:01,076
Thank God for the time you had with them.

135
00:08:01,448 --> 00:08:02,514
That's allowed.

136
00:08:02,886 --> 00:08:06,089
The ache and the thanks
can sit at the same table.

137
00:08:07,211 --> 00:08:11,243
And if you worked last night so
everybody else could have today

138
00:08:11,243 --> 00:08:14,827
off, the plant crew, the
nurse, the gas station, the guy

139
00:08:14,827 --> 00:08:18,731
driving a truck at three in the
morning, this is for you too.

140
00:08:19,103 --> 00:08:23,539
Somebody is eating a hot meal today
because you were on that clock.

141
00:08:23,911 --> 00:08:24,854
Thank you.

142
00:08:25,226 --> 00:08:26,337
God saw it.

143
00:08:28,159 --> 00:08:30,252
So what would I ask of you today?

144
00:08:30,624 --> 00:08:32,109
Don't be one of the nine.

145
00:08:32,481 --> 00:08:33,504
Two things.

146
00:08:34,626 --> 00:08:37,370
First, when the table prayer comes, name

147
00:08:37,370 --> 00:08:40,182
something out loud, and make it specific.

148
00:08:40,554 --> 00:08:42,279
Skip family and food.

149
00:08:42,651 --> 00:08:44,769
Say the truck started this morning.

150
00:08:45,141 --> 00:08:46,574
Say the lights are on.

151
00:08:46,946 --> 00:08:50,902
Specific thanks is how you find
out how much you've been handed.

152
00:08:52,024 --> 00:08:56,747
Second, find one person and tell them
the actual thing they did for you.

153
00:08:57,119 --> 00:09:00,232
Something like, you drove
me to that appointment

154
00:09:00,232 --> 00:09:02,566
when you had your own mess going on.

155
00:09:02,938 --> 00:09:04,888
Watch what it does to their face.

156
00:09:06,710 --> 00:09:07,743
Let's pray.

157
00:09:08,865 --> 00:09:11,791
Father, we come to You
in the name of Jesus, and

158
00:09:11,791 --> 00:09:14,474
the first thing we want
to say is thank You.

159
00:09:14,846 --> 00:09:18,514
You are good, and Your mercy
has not run out on us once.

160
00:09:18,886 --> 00:09:23,754
Forgive us for the times we took the
gift and kept walking like the nine.

161
00:09:24,126 --> 00:09:26,968
Teach us to turn around and say it to You.

162
00:09:27,340 --> 00:09:30,352
Thank You for the food on
our tables, for the people

163
00:09:30,352 --> 00:09:33,596
sitting around them, and for
the work that put it there.

164
00:09:33,968 --> 00:09:36,419
For the ones working today so the rest of

165
00:09:36,419 --> 00:09:38,810
us could rest, we ask You to bless them.

166
00:09:39,182 --> 00:09:42,765
Where there's an empty chair,
thank You for the time we had.

167
00:09:43,137 --> 00:09:48,327
Put a thankful spirit in every home,
and let it last well past this holiday.

168
00:09:48,699 --> 00:09:50,748
In Jesus' name, amen.

169
00:09:51,870 --> 00:09:56,260
If this blessed you, type amen, and
send it to a friend who needs it.

170
00:09:56,632 --> 00:10:00,090
Hit like and subscribe so
you don't miss the next one.

171
00:10:00,462 --> 00:10:03,174
Happy Thanksgiving,
and have a blessed day.

